# 15. SECURITY THREAT MODEL

| Threat | Severity | Required mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| Privilege escalation | Critical | Server-side Firebase verification and trusted RBAC |
| Unauthorized image access | High | Private bucket and signed URLs |
| Audit manipulation | Critical | Append-only permissions and hash chain |
| Duplicate submissions | Medium | Idempotency and unique constraints |
| SQL injection | High | Parameterized ORM queries |
| Malicious file uploads | High | Magic-byte checks and image decoding |
| GPS spoofing | Medium | Geographic validation and review |
| AI prompt injection | High | Treat user content as untrusted input |
| Invalid AI outputs | High | Schema validation and deterministic rules |
| Unauthorized dispatch | Critical | Backend human approval hard gate |
| Queue replay | Medium | Idempotent jobs and attempt tracking |
| Credential leakage | Critical | Server-side secret management |
| Notification abuse | Medium | Rate limits and authorization |
| Denial of service | High | Rate limits, upload caps and timeouts |

Security tests must verify both positive and negative access scenarios.

