# 16. TESTING AND ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

## 16.1 Build and code quality

- TypeScript compilation succeeds.
- Lint succeeds.
- Production build succeeds.
- No secrets are included in client bundles.
- Existing responsive layouts remain functional.

## 16.2 Database

- Migrations apply cleanly.
- Seeding is idempotent.
- Foreign keys work.
- Unique constraints prevent duplicate upvotes.
- Invalid state values are rejected.
- Concurrent complaint submissions receive unique references.

## 16.3 Authentication

- Valid Firebase token succeeds.
- Expired token fails.
- Invalid token fails.
- Citizen cannot access admin APIs.
- User-submitted role changes are ignored.
- Official provisioning is audited.

## 16.4 Complaint workflow

- Complaint is saved persistently.
- Reference code is returned.
- Refreshing the browser preserves complaint data.
- Uploaded evidence is privately stored.
- Duplicate complaint candidates are linked safely.
- GPS outside supported pilot wards is rejected or reviewed.

## 16.5 Human approval gate

Test:

1. Submit a complaint.
2. Run AI recommendation.
3. Attempt dispatch without approval.
4. Verify HTTP 409 Conflict.
5. Approve using an authorized official.
6. Dispatch successfully.
7. Verify audit record creation.

## 16.6 AI and IBM

- Gemini request succeeds using an actually available model.
- Granite request succeeds using an actually available model.
- Orchestrate invokes a deployed skill with real authentication.
- Structured output is validated.
- Provider failures are recorded.
- Invalid outputs cannot change official state.
- Fallback execution is labelled accurately.

## 16.7 Queue recovery

- Worker crash triggers retry.
- Duplicate job delivery does not duplicate business operations.
- Exhausted jobs enter failed state.
- Client complaint submission does not hang while AI runs.

## 16.8 Audit verification

- Every relevant state change produces an audit record.
- Runtime application credentials cannot update or delete audit entries.
- Modification of a record breaks verification.
- Chain sequence and previous hashes are validated.

## 16.9 User experience

Test at:
- 360px mobile.
- 390px mobile.
- Tablet.
- Laptop.
- Desktop.

Preserve:
- Navy/blue design.
- Existing typography.
- SafeImage fallbacks.
- Existing layout and component structure.

